{
  "source": "videos/layers-v4.mp4",
  "duration": 158.912,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.02,
      "end": 4.98,
      "text": "Have you ever read a sentence in a book that made absolutely no sense until you read it"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.98,
      "end": 6.3,
      "text": "a second or third time?"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.6,
      "end": 9.86,
      "text": "Look at this diagram of a confusing sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.46,
      "end": 12.22,
      "text": "The horse raced past the barn fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.86,
      "end": 14.78,
      "text": "At first, the grammar seems broken."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.34,
      "end": 16.72,
      "text": "You try different interpretations."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.44,
      "end": 18.22,
      "text": "Did a barn fall?"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.68,
      "end": 20.26,
      "text": "Did the horse race past afterward?"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.92,
      "end": 24.9,
      "text": "Finally, you realize someone raced a horse past a barn, and then it fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.64,
      "end": 28.78,
      "text": "Your comprehension of the sentence relies on each repeated pass."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.3,
      "end": 33.44,
      "text": "With every read, you update the meaning of the words until the whole thought makes sense."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.0,
      "end": 36.62,
      "text": "AI doesn't read the way we do."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.06,
      "end": 40.92,
      "text": "Instead, it processes your text through a mathematical stack called a neural network."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.46,
      "end": 43.72,
      "text": "This shows how neural network layers are structured."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.42,
      "end": 49.44,
      "text": "Inside each, attention and transformation update your words' numerical representations,"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.02,
      "end": 52.1,
      "text": "passing them sequentially to the next layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.74,
      "end": 55.14,
      "text": "The bottom table shows a word's initial state."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.56,
      "end": 60.32,
      "text": "As these values move through the layers to the end, the numbers shift at every stage."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.0,
      "end": 65.78,
      "text": "These shifting decimal values are the machine's version of a human rereading a sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.5,
      "end": 69.28,
      "text": "The changing math represents a sharpening of meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.0,
      "end": 75.7,
      "text": "We can see exactly how this mathematical meaning resolves by tracing one specific word through"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.7,
      "end": 76.26,
      "text": "the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.94,
      "end": 81.94,
      "text": "The cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm because it was tired."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.44,
      "end": 84.66,
      "text": "Focus on the ambiguous word, it."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.34,
      "end": 88.02,
      "text": "Its starting numbers don't reveal the pronoun's reference."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.7,
      "end": 94.6,
      "text": "But moving through layers 1 and 2, the numbers update, capturing specific mathematical connections"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.6,
      "end": 97.34,
      "text": "to cat, building over successive layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.8,
      "end": 101.66,
      "text": "Finally, the results mathematically conclude, it refers to cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.36,
      "end": 107.96,
      "text": "This step-by-step mathematical journey is how AI builds contextual connections that human"
    },
    {
      "start": 107.96,
      "end": 109.06,
      "text": "readers make instantly."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.06,
      "end": 114.86,
      "text": "Exactly how many layers are required in a real-world AI model."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.52,
      "end": 120.98,
      "text": "Tech companies rarely share their exact designs, but published models often use dozens and"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.98,
      "end": 123.76,
      "text": "sometimes well over a hundred distinct layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.46,
      "end": 129.74,
      "text": "If it takes multiple layers just to link a pronoun to a noun, more nuanced language"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.74,
      "end": 131.54,
      "text": "needs even more room to work."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.18,
      "end": 138.44,
      "text": "AI uses these dozens of extra steps to untangle the relationships behind sarcasm, story twists,"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.44,
      "end": 139.9,
      "text": "and complicated reasoning."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.62,
      "end": 143.98,
      "text": "Every additional layer demands more computing power and time."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.02,
      "end": 149.08,
      "text": "Developers have to balance the intelligence of their model against the cost of running it."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.48,
      "end": 156.74,
      "text": "Ultimately, meaning builds up, layer by layer, with attention and transformation, dozens"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.74,
      "end": 157.4,
      "text": "of times."
    }
  ],
